 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the public service law, in relation to responsibility for\ncable bills after a disconnection or downgrade in service",
    "basePrintNo": "S493",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S493-2023",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 31,
       "fullName": "Robert Jackson",
       "imgName": "1050_Robert_Jackson.jpg",
       "incumbent": true,
       "memberId": 1230,
       "sessionMemberId": 2017,
       "sessionYear": 2023,
       "shortName": "JACKSON"
      },
      {
       "alternate": false,
       "chamber": "SENATE",
       "districtCode": 52,
       "fullName": "Lea Webb",
       "imgName": "1332_Lea_Webb.jpg",
       "incumbent": true,
       "memberId": 1515,
       "sessionMemberId": 1878,
       "sessionYear": 2023,
       "shortName": "WEBB"
      }
     ],
     "size": 2
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §224-b, Pub Serv L",
    "lawSection": "Public Service Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S493\n\nSPONSOR: COMRIE\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the public service law, in relation to responsibility\nfor cable bills after a disconnection or downgrade in service\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill would provide a cable company customer the option to receive a\nprorated refund or billing in the event of a disconnection or downgrade.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one of the bill amends 224-b of the public service law as it\nrelates to limiting the services of a cable company customer is liable\nfor to services incurred up to a requested disconnection or downgrade of\nservice. A customer would be entitled to receive a prorated refund for a\ndisconnection or a billing credit for a downgrade.\n\nSection two of the bill relates to the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nCable companies do not offer prorated refunds for services that have\nbeen disconnected; leaving customers paying for services they no longer\nhave. Often cable bills are paid in advance for services so any discon-\nnection before the end of the billing cycle will result in the customer\npaying for services they are not using. This bill provides parity with\ncustomers by requiring cable companies to provide refunds on a pro rata\nbasis for when the disconnection becomes effective.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\n2022: S7457A\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
